\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces (Example 1) Posterior distributions (red) of the odds ratio (admission of males vs. females) using noisy (i.e. privacy-protected) data. Left panel: correct Bayesian inference using dapper which takes into account the privacy mechanism; Right panel: naive Bayesian inference treating the noisy data as noise-free. Blue distribution in both panels reflect the true posterior distribution if the analysis were to be conducted on the confidential data.}}{9}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:post-or-compare}{{3}{9}{(Example 1) Posterior distributions (red) of the odds ratio (admission of males vs. females) using noisy (i.e. privacy-protected) data. Left panel: correct Bayesian inference using dapper which takes into account the privacy mechanism; Right panel: naive Bayesian inference treating the noisy data as noise-free. Blue distribution in both panels reflect the true posterior distribution if the analysis were to be conducted on the confidential data}{figure.caption.5}{}}
