\newlabel{fig:post-or-compare-dg}{{5}{11}{(Example 2) Posterior distributions (red) of the odds ratio (admission of males vs. females) using noisy (i.e. privacy-protected) data. Left panel: correct Bayesian inference using dapper which takes into account the privacy mechanism; Right panel: naive Bayesian inference treating the noisy data as noise-free. Blue distribution in both panels reflect the true posterior distribution if the analysis were to be conducted on the confidential data}{figure.caption.8}{}}
