\newlabel{fig:regression-compare}{{6}{15}{(Example 3) The red densities represent the posteriors of the regression coefficient that come from applying the naive analysis to the privitized data. The blue densities are the privacy aware posterior distributions. The dashed lines are the true coefficient values}{figure.caption.9}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces (Example 3) This plot compares the posteriors that would arise from applying the naive, privacy blind analysis to the confidential and privitized data. The red densities represent the posterior of the coefficient under the confidential data. The blue densities are the posterior distributions that would arise from using the privitized data. The dashed lines are the true coefficient values.}}{15}{figure.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:regression-data-compare}{{7}{15}{(Example 3) This plot compares the posteriors that would arise from applying the naive, privacy blind analysis to the confidential and privitized data. The red densities represent the posterior of the coefficient under the confidential data. The blue densities are the posterior distributions that would arise from using the privitized data. The dashed lines are the true coefficient values}{figure.caption.10}{}}
